  "summary": "New Arabidopsis and crop studies map transcriptional, epigenetic and post-translational nodes that link ABA, JA and ROS to stress tolerance.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is regulatory control of hormone metabolism and ROS signaling under abiotic and biotic stress. On the ABA axis, GhNAC029 represses GhNCED1 to lower ABA and drought tolerance in cotton. In Brassica, promoter methylation of BraCYP707A3.A02 blocks BraBPC2.A08 binding, shifting ABA catabolism and clubroot resistance. Peroxisomal H2O2 homeostasis rebalances ABA/GA metabolism during Arabidopsis germination under water stress. JA appears in organ-specific form under combined heat and phosphate starvation (JA-Ile up in roots, JA down in shoots) and in ANAC030-driven leaf senescence. Post-translational mechanisms also feature. H2S persulfidation and PRMT5-dependent LSm4 methylation couple H2S signaling to alternative splicing in stomatal closure. In apple, MxMPK4-1 phosphorylates MxME3-7 at S201 to enhance ROS-mediated iron-deficiency responses. Other items extend the theme to clock (RVE4/6/8) control of osmotic and salt responses, miR159a–BrMYB12 regulation of raffinose-linked thermotolerance, and MAPK-associated salt relief by melatonin plus selenium nanoparticles.",
